To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to ensure that for every index greater than the specified index and less than the size of the list, the element at that index remains unchanged unless it was initially null. 

We can use the `\forall` quantifier to express this condition. Here's the assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); (\old(this.get(i)) == null || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>

This asserts that for all indices `i` such that `index < i < old size`, the element at index `i` either remains unchanged or was initially null.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); (\old(this.get(i)) == null || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
